===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[design]] [[flaw]] in [[computer]] [[system]]s that [[represent]]ed [[year]]s as two [[digit]]s (e.g. ''84'' for 1984), which could cause date calculations to fail if they involved years later than 1999.
#* {{RQ:Independent|author=Lizzy Buchan|title={{w|Boris Johnson}} says Trump could handle Brexit better and warns of 'meltdown' in explosive leaked recording|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180607212531/https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/politics/boris-johnson-recording-trump-brexit-dinner-party-tory-theresa-may-a8388686.html|date=7 June 2018|passage=Mr Johnson also said the Northern Irish border row had been blown out of proportion and compared fears over disruption over vital goods coming into the UK to "pure '''millennium bug''' stuff".}}

